From 75d0a9b7064fc26c065de28f8b020ff1cf1944fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeffrey Frederick <5095066+jeffreyfrederick@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:47:52 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] Report per-phase frame timings from the winit backend

Add `FrameTimings` / `FramePhase` (vizia_core::context) so apps and tools
can see where frame time goes: events (incl. timers), style, layout,
make-current, draw traversal, Skia flush and present. Backends report
phases with `BackendContext::record_frame_phase` and mark a presented
frame with `finish_frame`; apps read the last completed frame via
`Context::frame_timings()` / `EventContext::frame_timings()`.

The winit backend now records all phases; `WinState::swap_buffers`
returns the flush and present durations. Overhead is a handful of
`Instant::now()` calls per loop iteration.

Tested: ChipDAW GUI prototype F3 overlay and per-frame CSV log show
plausible, stable values (e.g. 43-clip demo: draw 2.5 ms, flush 1.3 ms).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
